abstract: >
  A computational pipeline (six notebooks in five numbered folders) that curates T-cell assay data from
  IEDB and CEDAR, verifies peptides against UniProt reference sequences,
  annotates MHC class I/II binding, engineers sequence, physicochemical,
  MHC-binding, and ESM-2 protein language model features, trains an
  explainable weighted ensemble classifier (logistic regression, SVM,
  tree ensembles, and XGBoost) under leakage-aware nested cross-validation,
  and validates the resulting model on an independent external peptide set.
  Four supplementary analyses (folders 06-09) accompany the pipeline: a
  benchmark against NetMHCpan/NetMHCIIpan rank, PRIME 2.1, the IEDB
  immunogenicity tool and simple baselines; a feature-block ablation with an
  ESM-2 redundancy analysis; and sensitivity analyses of the sequence-identity,
  label-confidence and cluster-consensus thresholds.
